  "spoken": "In one minute, the Moon falls five metres. An apple falls that far in one second Isaac Newton worked out why. The Moon is 60 times further from the Earth's centre than we are, so the pull on it is 60 times 60 weaker, 3,600 times. And the numbers matched. One pull for apples and Moons.",
